# Slice 284: `@: p Inner \q` with no comma is the path `Inner\q` whatever Inner holds, and Inner has no field q: refused at the declaration (VALUE-PATH-BY-FIELD-PRESENCE).
# Before, the missing field turned the same fields into a requirement and a dereference; `@: p Inner, \q` writes those (tests/dyn/comma_boundary.lm2).
Inner:
    int: v 3
end: Inner
@: r Inner Inner
@@: q Inner @ r
@: p Inner \q
send: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
